ero. The post-commit stream path at provider_failure_runtime_policy.rs:804 has the same unnormalized action construction.","remediation":"Apply the typed internal policy exactly once before every path enters record_provider_key_failure_action, including direct runtime and post-commit stream failures, or move that normalization into the unique provider-health action owner so callers cannot bypass it. Add regression coverage for direct 400/statusless failures and direct 401/403 threshold behavior."},{"severity":"P1","file":"docs/architecture/v3-verification-map.yml","line":31,"rule":"Required verification evidence must accompany a high-risk provider health change","evidence":"The affected feature v3.provider_key_health_model_granularity is marked source_controlled_runtime_pending_live_replay and declares npm run test:v3-provider-health-contract plus resource-map, module-boundary, binding, red-fixture, and diff checks as required gates. The related v3.provider_global_cooldown_persistence feature also declares a required persistence contract gate. The supplied commit scope contains source and test changes but no bound execution receipt, test result, architecture-gate result, or live replay evidence, so the required acceptance evidence for this high-risk cooldown/health change is not established.","remediation":"Run and attach receipts for every applicable mapped gate against commit 15b6873a0, including provider-health and global-cooldown persistence contract tests, resource/module/binding checks, red fixtures, and diff check; provide live replay evidence where required by the feature completion boundary."}]}
